WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.112 --> 00:00:04.337
The greatest engineering stories are not stories about magic.

2
00:00:04.412 --> 00:00:08.162
They are stories about problems made understandable.

3
00:00:08.262 --> 00:00:11.312
A flying Roadster demonstration can capture the imagination.

4
00:00:11.362 --> 00:00:14.807
The equations tell us what it might mean.

5
00:00:14.857 --> 00:00:19.039
And the work ahead tells us what remains to be done.

6
00:00:19.463 --> 00:00:23.388
The future does not arrive because someone says it will.

7
00:00:23.438 --> 00:00:28.563
It arrives when imagination meets experiment, discipline and proof.

8
00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:34.238
This is Beyond Gravity. A dramatic engineering demonstration can inspire people to

9
00:00:34.288 --> 00:00:37.761
explore questions they might never otherwise ask.

10
00:00:38.221 --> 00:00:44.196
But spectacle becomes valuable education only when it leads to the right explanations,

11
00:00:44.271 --> 00:00:50.296
careful uncertainty and the discipline to distinguish assumptions from observations.

12
00:00:50.371 --> 00:00:54.396
Can such machines safely support routine travel?

13
00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:57.377
Can the energy and infrastructure budgets work?

14
00:00:57.759 --> 00:01:01.409
How do they behave after failures and in difficult weather?

15
00:01:01.484 --> 00:01:04.634
Those questions are not signs of pessimism.

16
00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:09.104
They are precisely what meaningful engineering must investigate before the

17
00:01:09.129 --> 00:01:15.179
extraordinary becomes normal. Gravity was never an obstacle to be wished away.

18
00:01:15.254 --> 00:01:17.870
It is a force to understand and work with.

19
00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:23.555
When every drawing, simulation and test teaches us something real, even a brief

20
00:01:23.655 --> 00:01:27.180
glimpse of the future becomes more interesting.

21
00:01:27.255 --> 00:01:32.080
The story continues with the next measurement, the next prototype, and the next

22
00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:32.867
question.
